+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static homepage; no build step or dependencies. Open through your existing static hosting setup.
+
+## SMS authentication
+
+By default the homepage runs in visibly labeled preview mode. No SMS is sent and no account is authenticated. Enter an international phone number (for example `+1 555 123 4567`), then use `123456` to preview verification. Preview codes expire after five minutes. Both Rewards and Online order use the same form.
+
+To enable real authentication, add this to the HTML head after deploying your SMS backend:
+
+```html
+<meta name="sms-auth-api" content="/api/auth/sms">
+```
+
+The same-origin service must expose these JSON endpoints:
+
+- `POST /api/auth/sms/send`: accepts `{phone, intent}` and returns `{challengeId}` only after requesting SMS delivery.
+- `POST /api/auth/sms/verify`: accepts `{phone, code, challengeId, intent}` and returns `{verified: true}` only after verification, establishing an authenticated session through a secure HttpOnly cookie. The client then navigates to `/rewards` or `/order-online`.
+
+Use non-2xx status codes for failures and `429` for throttling. The server must validate phone numbers, bind challenges to the requesting session and phone, enforce code expiry, one-time use, resend/attempt limits, and origin/CSRF protection. The 30-second client resend countdown is a usability aid, not a security boundary. Never trust client-side validation or the preview code in production.
+
+Send human-readable text and bind the message to the exact deployed hostname on its final line:
+
+```text
+Your Daily Grind sign-in code is 012345.
+
+@your-deployed-hostname.com #012345
+```
+
+Do not include a scheme, path, port, or trailing text on the final line. Generate real codes on the server. Production must use HTTPS. WebOTP starts before delivery, submits through native validation, and cancels on manual submit, resend, number/purpose changes, timeout, and navigation. Unsupported or denied WebOTP falls back to native `autocomplete="one-time-code"` and manual entry. The code uses a single labeled text input with a numeric keyboard, supports paste and leading zeroes, and announces errors/status to assistive technology.
+
+## Checks
+
+`node --check app.js` checks JavaScript syntax without starting a server.
